# Local resources (template)

Copy this file to `.ai/local.md` and fill it in. `local.md` is **gitignored** —
it records things that are true of *your machine only*, so that every AI agent
working here (Claude, Codex, Antigravity, …) can find the same local resources.

Rules:

- Machine-specific paths go here; everything repo-universal goes in
  [core.md](core.md).
- **No secrets.** No tokens, JWKs, passwords, or tenant credentials — not even
  "temporarily". Point at how to obtain them instead.
- Keep it short. It is a set of pointers, not documentation.

## AIC API reference

The verified AIC API doc set lives in the sibling project
[`agiledigital-labs/pingone-aic-manager`](https://github.com/agiledigital-labs/pingone-aic-manager)
under `docs/api/`. `core.md` explains why it is authoritative; record where your
checkout is:

```
<path-to>/pingone-aic-manager/docs/api/
```

If you don't have it: `git clone git@github.com:agiledigital-labs/pingone-aic-manager.git`
somewhere alongside this repo.

## Tenant

Which tenant you develop against, and how to get a token — the *method*, never
the token itself. For example, a helper script that shells out to an already
unlocked `aic` agent.

## Anything else machine-local

Other sibling checkouts, local tool builds, scratch directories.
